{
	chapter.231570DE6A7FCD52.title: "When Dungeons Arise"
	quest.0331AC0315EBB66D.quest_desc: ["Nestled among the trees, this lively tavern is usually a haven for villagers looking to unwind. Yet when the ale flows too freely, even the most peaceful patrons turn aggressive, defending their pub with surprising ferocity. Enter carefully or risk being caught in a drunken brawl."]
	quest.0331AC0315EBB66D.quest_subtitle: "Find a Greenwood Pub"
	quest.041A1C64A8468087.quest_desc: ["Suspended high in the sky, this arrowhead-shaped airship drifts on a massive aft propeller. Boarding is perilous, but those who succeed will witness its strange and fearsome inhabitants riding boar-like beasts, their eyeless faces obscured by ominous cages. Danger and mystery ride with them across the clouds."]
	quest.041A1C64A8468087.quest_subtitle: "Find a Heavenly Rider"
	quest.0B89EB36AC565461.quest_desc: ["Deep within this subterranean city, the heat of molten lava and the hum of industry dominate the air. The Nether’s influence is strong here, fueling forges and animating Forge Sentinels that patrol every corridor. Only those prepared for fire and steel will survive, and claim the treasures forged within."]
	quest.0B89EB36AC565461.quest_subtitle: "Find a Foundry"
	quest.0CE50A7F4F1A0E4D.quest_desc: ["ladder stretches skyward, disappearing into the clouds. At its top floats a strange, floating vessel. What secrets or dangers await above, none can say… except that the view alone is enough to make even the bravest adventurer’s stomach turn."]
	quest.0CE50A7F4F1A0E4D.quest_subtitle: "Find a Small Blimp"
	quest.14857DBF1DCBF100.quest_desc: ["Cresting the waves like a shadow of the past, this cursed vessel is crewed by skeletons that seem impossible to keep down. Every deck hides danger, every hold whispers of lost treasure and every strike you land may be fleeting. Only the bold (or the foolhardy) dare to face its relentless undead crew."]
	quest.14857DBF1DCBF100.quest_subtitle: "Find an Undead Pirate Ship"
	quest.188AAB5B74C6EAAE.quest_subtitle: "Discover an Infested Temple explorer map"
	quest.1C375606107C117F.quest_subtitle: "Find Keep Kayra"
	quest.1CCA31D9352C60E6.quest_desc: ["Clustered around a towering central “grandmother” mushroom, these villages appear quaint from afar. Yet the villagers within are far more aggressive than their old-world counterparts, hiding a cunning fierceness beneath their colorful caps. Approach with caution as this village may welcome the unwary only to spring its traps."]
	quest.1CCA31D9352C60E6.quest_subtitle: "Find a mushroom village"
	quest.1CEF2A38948010A2.quest_desc: ["Out on the open seas, the &6Illagers&r have taken to the waves, commandeering massive galleys and swift corsairs. Their sails cast long shadows, and their cannons roar with fury. Only the bravest dare to board, for fortune favors those who seize it."]
	quest.1CEF2A38948010A2.quest_subtitle: "Find an Illager Corsair or an Illager Galley"
	quest.1F10BC33D22328BD.quest_desc: ["Time has claimed this once-sacred site, leaving its halls cracked and overgrown. Now, ghostly skeletons and trickster illusioners linger within, guarding little more than shadows of former glory. Though its dangers are real, the temple’s sturdy walls make it a tempting refuge for those seeking a foothold in this hostile world."]
	quest.1F10BC33D22328BD.quest_subtitle: "Find an Abandoned Temple"
	quest.21426F5EEC922866.quest_desc: ["Half-submerged in the oceans lie the petrified remains of a colossal beast, its skeletal form stretching farther than the eye can follow. Was it a creature of the deep, dragged ashore in ages past—or did it fall from the heavens themselves? No records remain, only questions carved into stone."]
	quest.21426F5EEC922866.quest_subtitle: "Find a Typhon"
	quest.2A0A01BE836BB2AB.quest_desc: ["A monument of grandeur and mystery, the Shiraz Palace sprawls in every direction, its halls twisting and turning beyond comprehension. Its purpose remains unknown, but its size and opulence are undeniable. Travelers beware: without a companion, it’s all too easy to lose your way in this labyrinthine estate."]
	quest.2A0A01BE836BB2AB.quest_subtitle: "Find the Shiraz Palace"
	quest.2A1B0386B7987DD3.quest_desc: ["Vast and dreamlike, the Aviary stretches high into wtilight sky, its halls divided into four whimsical quadrants. Each one unfolds as a surreal scene—bright, strange, and perilous in its own way. To wander here feels like stepping beyond reality itself. Is this the journey’s end… or just another beginning?"]
	quest.2A1B0386B7987DD3.quest_subtitle: "Find an Aviary"
	quest.2B70445E6CD99EDB.quest_desc: [
		"Strange structures have begun rising from the land. Mysterious dungeons, fortresses, and towers that pierce the skies. No one knows where they came from, only that they’re teeming with hostile creatures, forgotten treasures, and powerful secrets."
		""
		"Your task is to venture forth and uncover the mysteries of these ancient places. Each dungeon holds new dangers, but also the keys to survival: weapons, artifacts, and knowledge that will aid you in the trials ahead."
		""
		"Prepare yourself adventurer. &6Exploration&r and courage are the only ways to thrive in this world where the land itself rises against you."
	]
	quest.2DB4F395EA26DF4B.quest_subtitle: "Find a Coliseum"
	quest.2EFC5DBD8122A0AE.quest_desc: ["Far below the surface lies a twisted network of chambers, where the air is thick with disease and shadow. Once a place of treatment, it now resembles a burial ground for forgotten rulers, its halls echoing with the whispers of those long lost. Only the brave (or the desperate) dare to tread these haunted corridors."]
	quest.2EFC5DBD8122A0AE.quest_subtitle: "Find a Plague Asylum"
	quest.3D1C0F80B74B27D5.quest_subtitle: "Arrive at a Lighthouse"
	quest.3ECA226F08D5195F.quest_desc: ["Hidden among hills and valleys, the monastery stands as a quiet refuge in a world of rising danger. Here, villagers tend to simple lives of prayer and work, untouched by Illager conquest. Though the halls hold little in the way of treasure, their sturdy walls and peaceful company make this an ideal sanctuary for weary adventurers."]
	quest.3ECA226F08D5195F.quest_subtitle: "Find a Monastery"
	quest.4118927D9D079DC8.quest_desc: ["Rising like jagged thorns from the ground, these massive towers are defended by skeletons entwined with deadly roses. Each level is heavily fortified, and flying rose guards patrol the skies above. Only those who ascend to the top will claim the treasures and secrets hidden within."]
	quest.4118927D9D079DC8.quest_subtitle: "Visit the Thornborn Towers"
	quest.436231715C11E3BA.quest_desc: ["Scattered across the wilds, small bands of Illagers set up camp beneath their distinctive purple tents. Though their supplies are meager and their loot scarce, their presence is a warning, the Illagers’ reach grows wider with every outpost."]
	quest.436231715C11E3BA.quest_subtitle: "Find an Illager Campsite"
	quest.44D115281B0BFB75.quest_desc: ["Whispers speak of a &9flying vessel&r that hovers above the world, shimmering with strange energy. Few dare approach, for those who return tell of eerie lights, warped corridors, and guardians not of this realm. Seek it out, if you dare—and uncover the secrets hidden within its metallic shell."]
	quest.44D115281B0BFB75.quest_subtitle: "Find a Giant Mushroom"
	quest.4791FC0A2E834D85.quest_desc: ["Dark magics linger in the depths of these dungeons, woven into items, halls, and even the very air. Power awaits the bold, but so do twisted fates for the careless."]
	quest.4791FC0A2E834D85.quest_subtitle: "Find a Bathhouse"
	quest.4E4052F7EAD4FDD6.quest_desc: ["Bright banners and painted walls lure travelers closer, but inside these towering strongholds, chaos reigns. Each floor brims with bandits and traps, their laughter echoing as waves of foes pour from endless spawners. Conquer the towers, and their riches—and notoriety—are yours."]
	quest.4E4052F7EAD4FDD6.quest_subtitle: "Find the Bandit Towers"
	quest.509E9CA83FBC780E.quest_subtitle: "Find a Fishing Hut"
	quest.5100CFAD43E7D67A.quest_desc: ["Rising like a monument to conquest, this sprawling fortress serves as a bastion of Illager power. Its many levels are patrolled by raiders and spellcasters, their banners declaring dominion over the land. Within its halls lie chambers of wealth, guarded by Evokers whose magic is as deadly as their stares."]
	quest.5100CFAD43E7D67A.quest_subtitle: "Find an Illager Fort"
	quest.53AF2B722A69DCDC.quest_desc: ["Tucked away in the tall grass, this lonely house stands weathered and broken, its timbers groaning with age. Easy to overlook, it bears little more than the memory of those who once called it home. Still, even the smallest refuge can hold a story."]
	quest.53AF2B722A69DCDC.quest_subtitle: "Find a Small Prairie House"
	quest.541BBC35DA4F0B73.quest_desc: ["Sprouting from a cluster of towering fungi, this outpost of miners has carved their livelihood into the surface world. Ruthless and territorial, they will defend their claim with tooth and nail. Whether the giant mushrooms shield them from the sun or serve some darker purpose, none can say. One truth remains certain: the mine runs rich with ore, for those bold enough to claim it."]
	quest.541BBC35DA4F0B73.quest_subtitle: "Find a Mushroom Mine"
	quest.5C12F4CC1F6F6C32.quest_desc: ["Looming among the clouds, this massive airship bristles with defenses and hostile crew. Phantom-mounted fiends circle overhead, while fish-like raiders astride hoglins stalk the decks. Boarding it is no small feat. Tthose who triumph will etch their name among the few who dared challenge the skies."]
	quest.5C12F4CC1F6F6C32.quest_subtitle: "Find a Heavenly Challenger"
	quest.63116691C92FD576.quest_desc: ["A quiet spring hidden among the hills, its waters swirl mysteriously in the bottomless well. Travelers speak of subtle blessings for those brave enough to approach. Some even report a modest burst of speed for journeys ahead. Whether magic or rumor, the well offers a curious advantage to explorers."]
	quest.63116691C92FD576.quest_subtitle: "Find a Wishing Well"
	quest.6447492FAA873F93.quest_desc: ["Suspended in the sky, this floating steampunk city glows in hues of orange and green. Strange, gear-driven inhabitants roam its platforms, each dominated by a singular central eye or monocle. Enter with caution, this mechanical hive is as clever as it is imposing, and its secrets are tightly guarded."]
	quest.6447492FAA873F93.quest_subtitle: "Find a Mechanical Nest"
	quest.67030CEFEC1CEF37.quest_desc: ["Driven from their villages, these hardy merchants now wander the wilds, taking shelter beneath simple cyan and brown tents. Though weary from exile, they still offer trade and refuge to travelers brave enough to seek them out. In a world rising with danger, such camps are rare havens of trust."]
	quest.67030CEFEC1CEF37.quest_subtitle: "Find a Merchant Campsite"
	quest.6858E25E510AE0FA.quest_desc: ["Drifting through the skies like a colossal squid, this otherworldly airship bristles with defenses. Phantom-riding monstrosities circle its hull, while fish-like warriors astride hoglins guard its decks. To face the Conqueror is to battle a skyborne legion. And only the strongest will claim victory."]
	quest.6858E25E510AE0FA.quest_subtitle: "Find a Heavenly Conqueror"
	quest.6A0237FADC519965.quest_desc: ["From a distance, it looks peaceful. Fields of golden wheat swaying beside a proud windmill. But don’t be deceived: the Illagers tend no crops for trade. Behind the rustic facade lies a nest of evil, their blades as sharp as the sickles they carry."]
	quest.6A0237FADC519965.quest_subtitle: "Find an Illager Windmill"
	quest.6BFE5D35265080E6.quest_desc: ["A sprawling underground stronghold, the Scorched Mines radiate in four cardinal directions from a central dome. Heat and shadows fill the tunnels, and danger lurks at every turn. Brave adventurers who navigate its branching paths may uncover riches, but only if they survive the hazards within."]
	quest.6BFE5D35265080E6.quest_subtitle: "Find the Scorched Mines"
	quest.6CB5ACBAAED66871.quest_desc: ["Shaped from the stem and cap of a giant fungus, this whimsical dwelling offers a rare touch of charm in a perilous world. Lightly guarded and easy to claim, the mushroom house makes for a delightful refuge, perfect for any adventurer who’s ever dreamed of calling a mushroom home."]
	quest.6CB5ACBAAED66871.quest_subtitle: "Find a Mushroom House"
	quest.70327C3AC547B354.quest_desc: ["Marked by its dark prismarine and yellow terracotta roof, this temple has long since fallen to corruption. Inside, swarms of spider-like creatures creep through its halls, striking with venom and ferocity. To enter is to step into a nest where every shadow crawls."]
	quest.70327C3AC547B354.quest_subtitle: "Find an Infested Temple"
	quest.7052C9A5A804E866.quest_desc: ["A riot of color rises from the wilderness, marking the territory of a cunning band of raiders. Their homes are bright and inviting, but enter at your own risk. These defenders strike fast and often. Those who prevail will find spoils and secrets hidden among the lively façades."]
	quest.7052C9A5A804E866.quest_subtitle: "Find a Bandit Village"
	quest.73D5EE5238C37982.quest_desc: ["In the wilds rests the skeletal form of a great creature. its skeleton stretching skyward like branches of pale bone. Whether a relic of forgotten myth or a beast once hunted to extinction, none can say. Its silent frame endures as a monument to creatures long lost."]
	quest.73D5EE5238C37982.quest_subtitle: "Find a Ceryneian Hind"
	quest.76DAECF378BA3F19.quest_desc: ["Far beneath the surface lies a labyrinth of rails and tunnels, carved by long-forgotten hands. The air is thick with dust and danger. Creatures lurk in the shadows, and the echoes of minecarts rattle through the dark. Yet for those who endure, veins of treasure and hidden chambers make the descent worthwhile."]
	quest.76DAECF378BA3F19.quest_subtitle: "Find a Mining System"

	quest.D2990D87FF3885AC.title: "Two Books, Two Purposes"
	quest.D2990D87FF3885AC.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.D2990D87FF3885AC.quest_desc: [
		"Educational reference only. Item values, recipes, gear grades and mod compatibility may change after the first full AO test."
		"Newcomers / navigation"
		"Adventure Journal (Questlog) tells you what is happening: which place you discovered, which challenge looks appropriate, and what optional journey has just become available. Field Manual (FTB Quests) answers the questions that interrupt an adventure: what an item does, where a spell comes from, how a crafting system works and what a particular button means."
		"Both books are meant to be browsed, not finished in a strict order. The manual can be opened when a Questlog entry points to a mechanic you have not learned. Reading an explanation should not automatically grant the same reward a player receives for completing the associated adventure."
		"Try this: Find the topic for your current tool or spell, then return to the Adventure Journal."
	]
	task.0798826C96206CD5.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.D2991087FF388AC5.title: "JEI: Your Recipe Encyclopedia"
	quest.D2991087FF388AC5.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.D2991087FF388AC5.quest_desc: [
		"Educational reference only. Item values, recipes, gear grades and mod compatibility may change after the first full AO test."
		"Newcomers / items"
		"An unfamiliar material may be useful long before its purpose is obvious. JEI helps answer two different questions: How do I craft this? and What can I make with it? That distinction matters with modded components that have dozens of possible recipes."
		"Use the search bar for a name or ingredient, hover the result to inspect details, and use the recipe and uses actions listed in your controls. Common defaults may be changed by the modpack, so the on-screen controls take priority. Some recipes also require special stations, rituals or progression. A recipe appearing in JEI does not guarantee it is currently accessible."
		"Try this: Inspect a loot item, then look up both one recipe that makes it and one recipe that consumes it."
	]
	task.07987F6C962067BC.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.D2990F87FF388912.title: "Shield, Off-Hand and Unusual Attacks"
	quest.D2990F87FF388912.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.D2990F87FF388912.quest_desc: [
		"Educational reference only. Item values, recipes, gear grades and mod compatibility may change after the first full AO test."
		"Newcomers / combat"
		"A shield occupies the off-hand and can prevent damage from many ordinary attacks when raised at the right time. It does not make you invulnerable. Some enemies use magic, area attacks, knockback or attacks whose behavior differs from vanilla Minecraft."
		"Before a dungeon, practice using your shield against familiar mobs. Check whether your weapon has unusual timing, reach or a special action. If a monster has a telegraphed move, moving out of its path may be safer than standing still and relying on armor."
		"Try this: Block a basic attack safely, then practice moving while keeping your retreat route clear."
	]
	task.0798806C9620696F.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.D2990A87FF388093.title: "Equipment Slots and Combat Supports"
	quest.D2990A87FF388093.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.D2990A87FF388093.quest_desc: [
		"Educational reference only. Item values, recipes, gear grades and mod compatibility may change after the first full AO test."
		"Gear / Curios"
		"Some items work simply by sitting in an equipment slot; others activate on hit, after damage, on movement or when triggered manually. Two objects can both be called accessories without fitting into two usable slots. Always check the actual Curios or other equipment layout rather than assuming that carrying them grants their effects."
		"AO grades combat-support items by how much they help in a fight, not only by rarity. The early Tier 2 benchmark is enchanted diamond armor around Protection III plus two compatible A-grade combat supports. A powerful Origin passive does not substitute for either item. Some exceptional EX-grade effects still need balance testing."
		"Try this: Compare the effects, cooldowns and occupied slots of two supports in the AO Gear Atlas."
	]
	task.07987D6C96206456.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.D2990987FF387EE0.title: "Lootr, Shared Loot and Multiplayer Courtesy"
	quest.D2990987FF387EE0.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.D2990987FF387EE0.quest_desc: [
		"Educational reference only. Item values, recipes, gear grades and mod compatibility may change after the first full AO test."
		"Newcomers / multiplayer"
		"Some dungeon containers may provide personal loot for each player, while other containers behave as ordinary shared storage. Learn the difference before the first multiplayer expedition. A player reaching a chest first should not automatically mean everybody else loses access—but a personal loot feature must not be assumed for every chest and inventory."
		"Keep the group informed about especially rare finds, and be cautious around equipment dropped after death. A server may have additional rules for tombstones, claims and borrowed gear; the Field Manual should describe the current AO setup rather than generic defaults."
		"Try this: With a friend, inspect a known personal-loot container and a normal chest to recognize the difference."
	]
	task.07987E6C96206609.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.D2990C87FF3883F9.title: "Waystones, Maps and Returning Safely"
	quest.D2990C87FF3883F9.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.D2990C87FF3883F9.quest_desc: [
		"Educational reference only. Item values, recipes, gear grades and mod compatibility may change after the first full AO test."
		"Navigation"
		"A map marker helps you remember a place; a Waystone provides another kind of travel convenience when it has been discovered or configured. Neither replaces expedition planning. A portal that leads somewhere unfamiliar may require a different route back, and a waypoint does not guarantee safety at its destination."
		"Record at least one home marker and label important portals clearly. When a major dungeon is too dangerous, save its location instead of forcing the fight. AO's planned Explorer's Journal will only show or export locations you have genuinely discovered."
		"Try this: Create a clearly named home waypoint and one marker for a distant landmark."
	]
	task.07987B6C962060F0.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.D2990B87FF388246.title: "Apotheosis: Affixes, Gems and Sockets"
	quest.D2990B87FF388246.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.D2990B87FF388246.quest_desc: [
		"Educational reference only. Item values, recipes, gear grades and mod compatibility may change after the first full AO test."
		"Advanced equipment"
		"Apotheosis adds another layer to equipment evaluation beyond its vanilla base type. An item can have special affixes, rarities, sockets or gem-related bonuses. Those modifiers are not interchangeable with ordinary enchantments, and stacking the wrong effects may produce a worse build than choosing two complementary ones."
		"Inspect each item's complete tooltip before salvaging or reforging it. Ask whether a modifier improves survivability, damage, mobility or a narrower trigger condition. A shiny rarity label is less informative than the actual benefit against an upcoming boss. The AO Gear Atlas will compare results using the installed 1.21.1 Apotheosis configuration."
		"Try this: Compare two items of the same base material but with different affixes and explain why one suits your build better."
	]
	task.07987C6C962062A3.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.D2991687FF3894F7.title: "Apotheosis: Enchanting and Upgrading"
	quest.D2991687FF3894F7.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.D2991687FF3894F7.quest_desc: [
		"Educational reference only. Item values, recipes, gear grades and mod compatibility may change after the first full AO test."
		"Advanced equipment"
		"An enchanting setup is more than surrounding a table with generic bookshelves. This modpack may use additional shelf types and several interacting enchanting attributes. The right table configuration depends on whether you are trying to access stronger enchantments, control undesirable ones or use a particular modded item."
		"The manual should eventually show one actual AO-tested setup and explain what every displayed attribute does. Until we verify current configs, avoid copying a maximal build from a different Minecraft version. JEI recipes are the place to confirm which shelves and workstations are actually available."
		"Try this: Review the enchanting screen's attribute labels and locate the manual's tested starter arrangement."
	]
	task.0798896C962078BA.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.D2991587FF389344.title: "Relics: Effects, Activation and Growth"
	quest.D2991587FF389344.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.D2991587FF389344.quest_desc: [
		"Educational reference only. Item values, recipes, gear grades and mod compatibility may change after the first full AO test."
		"Relics / Artifacts"
		"Relics and Artifacts are not all passive bonuses. Some ask you to press a key, some depend on a cooldown, and some gain functionality or strength through the mod's own leveling or charging rules. A useful passive that triggers constantly can be more valuable than an impressive special ability you seldom remember to activate."
		"The Field Manual will document each important support's slot, activation method, level behavior and any known conflicts with other equipment. The Adventure Journal should reward using a meaningful relic well—not endlessly collecting every relic in the pack."
		"Try this: Pick one item you own, identify exactly when it helps, and verify it can be equipped in your current layout."
	]
	task.07988A6C96207A6D.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.12979A16AD0B0814.title: "Iron's Spellbooks: Schools and Casting"
	quest.12979A16AD0B0814.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.12979A16AD0B0814.quest_desc: [
		"Educational reference only. Item values, recipes, gear grades and mod compatibility may change after the first full AO test."
		"Magic / spellbooks"
		"Spellbooks hold spells with particular costs, cast requirements and school-related properties. When a new spell looks weaker than expected, consider whether the problem is its level, available mana, cast time, cooldown or the enemy's defenses. In combat, learning to recognize when a spell is ready is as important as unlocking one with a larger number."
		"The manual should contain the exact AO-tested routes for finding scrolls, upgrading books and understanding school interactions. It should also distinguish spells added by Traveloptics or other addons from the core Iron's Spellbooks spell roster."
		"Try this: Equip a basic book, read the mana cost of one spell and test it against an ordinary enemy before fighting a wizard boss."
	]
	task.089283831919091F.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.12979B16AD0B09C7.title: "Ars Nouveau: Build a Spell with Glyphs"
	quest.12979B16AD0B09C7.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.12979B16AD0B09C7.quest_desc: [
		"Educational reference only. Item values, recipes, gear grades and mod compatibility may change after the first full AO test."
		"Magic / Ars Nouveau"
		"Ars Nouveau lets players compose magical effects rather than merely choose a finished attack. A spell begins with how it targets something, then adds effects and modifiers to shape what happens. Small combinations often provide enormous utility: moving something, placing light or helping with ordinary exploration can matter more than a large damage spell."
		"Start with a simple, reproducible spell and confirm its resource cost. Only then add further glyphs or complex rituals. The Field Manual should provide step-by-step examples in the actual pinned AO version, with a clear distinction between combat spells, utility spells and automation."
		"Try this: Build a basic useful spell and explain which component selects a target and which creates the result."
	]
	task.089282831919076C.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.12979C16AD0B0B7A.title: "When a Dungeon is Above Your Tier"
	quest.12979C16AD0B0B7A.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.12979C16AD0B0B7A.quest_desc: [
		"Educational reference only. Item values, recipes, gear grades and mod compatibility may change after the first full AO test."
		"Encounter readiness"
		"AO tiers indicate how demanding a location is expected to be. They are a preparation guide, not an invisible wall. A Tier 6 arena may be discovered while you are still wearing Tier 2 equipment; the journal should record the find and allow you to return later instead of punishing curiosity."
		"Before entering, compare your armor, supports, damage options, resistances and escape route to the boss dossier. Some encounters require the right response to a mechanic, not just better numbers. Discovery, conquest and optional mastery are different kinds of progress."
		"Try this: Identify a discovered dungeon's provisional difficulty tier and one improvement you want before entering."
	]
	task.0892858319190C85.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.12979D16AD0B0D2D.title: "The Dreamscape and Its Native Systems"
	quest.12979D16AD0B0D2D.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.12979D16AD0B0D2D.quest_desc: [
		"Educational reference only. Item values, recipes, gear grades and mod compatibility may change after the first full AO test."
		"Optional mod / NeoPasterDream"
		"NeoPasterDream includes unusual world rules, equipment and puzzle interactions. Its dream dimension is not just another place to mine familiar ores. The player's first step should be to examine the native guidebook and learn how to travel safely; more specialized workshop and puzzle chapters can then become optional."
		"The current AO historical JAR is version 0.9.6. Later web descriptions list additional realm content, so an instruction must not mention a dimension or recipe that this specific version cannot access. This manual should eventually show real photographs of the game's own GUI rather than generic mockups."
		"Try this: Find the version-specific guidebook, and distinguish which content is currently available from unfinished future features."
	]
	task.0892848319190AD2.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.12979616AD0B0148.title: "Enigmatic Legacy: The Choice of Curses"
	quest.12979616AD0B0148.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.12979616AD0B0148.quest_desc: [
		"Educational reference only. Item values, recipes, gear grades and mod compatibility may change after the first full AO test."
		"Optional mod / Enigmatic Legacy"
		"Enigmatic equipment can be explored without automatically agreeing to the Ring of the Seven Curses. AO treats the ordinary artifact route and the cursed route as separate optional adventures. The cursed route is for players who deliberately want stronger constraints and unfamiliar risk; it is never a requirement for the main campaign."
		"Before a player intentionally accepts the curse, the manual should show the exact current restrictions, whether its effects can be reversed, and which items really require the cursed state. Neither picking up a ring nor opening a quest should secretly trigger that choice."
		"Try this: Compare two known non-cursed relics and read the full warning before deciding whether the optional challenge interests you."
	]
	task.08927F8319190253.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	chapter.15F13AC2B83226D6.title: "Ambient Odyssey — Field Manual"
	quest.8EEF3241E33CD8FC.title: "Ten things worth knowing before your first proper expedition"
	quest.8EEF3241E33CD8FC.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.8EEF3241E33CD8FC.quest_desc: [
		"Optional practical tips. This page gives no quest rewards and is not required to progress."
		"1. JEI is your in-game encyclopedia. Hover an unfamiliar item, use R for its recipe and U for everything it can become. Searching the Uses of a boss drop can reveal its whole crafting chain. JEI page / cheatsheet."
		"2. A backpack doesn't replace preparation. Leave space for rare loot, but also carry emergency blocks, food, light and a reliable way to return."
		"3. Mark major discoveries immediately. If a castle looks too dangerous, set a waypoint and leave. Finding it and defeating its guardian are different achievements."
		"4. A dungeon's danger is not always visible from outside. A gigantic structure might be survivable early, while a small chamber can house a strong boss. Use AO tier guidance before committing."
		"5. Have a retreat route. Don't jump blindly into a shaft, break your last way back or set a bed/respawn point without considering distance from home."
		"6. Enchanting and armor matter early. AO's intended Tier 2 benchmark is enchanted diamond armor around Protection III plus two concurrently usable A-grade combat-support items, not only a fancy weapon."
		"7. Passive accessories aren't automatically active in your inventory. Read the item, find its actual Curios/Accessories slot, and test whether it triggers passively, under conditions or by key press."
		"8. Different dimensions often change the rules. Don't assume your Overworld gear, food, fall protection or return portal strategy is appropriate everywhere."
		"9. Optional content stays optional. You don't need to finish every magic mod, dream realm or rare dungeon to enjoy the main AO progression."
		"10. Questlog and FTB have different jobs. Questlog follows the adventure; this Field Manual explains the systems and fixes confusing moments."
	]
	task.654629AA066B8C03.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.8EEF3541E33CDE15.title: "Inventory tricks that save hours"
	quest.8EEF3541E33CDE15.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.8EEF3541E33CDE15.quest_desc: [
		"Optional practical tips. This page gives no quest rewards and is not required to progress."
		"11. Quick-move stacks with Shift + Click. Use this to sort loot into chests fast. You can often move matching stacks with other standard inventory interactions; check the Keybind Cheatsheet."
		"12. Swap an item directly into a hotbar slot. Hover it inside your inventory and press the number of the intended slot. This is useful when preparing for a boss without dragging items across the screen."
		"13. Don't confuse dropping one item with dropping a whole stack. Q and Ctrl+Q are different. Accidental stack drops near lava and voids are painful."
		"14. JEI can chain recipes. If an ingredient is unfamiliar, click or hover it to trace backward through manufacturing steps, then use Back to return to the original target."
		"15. Filter JEI by source mod. Try searches such as @ars, @apotheosis, or a particular item name. Not every recipe is enabled in our final pack, so check tooltips and verified guides if something doesn't work."
		"16. Treat rare items as questions. Hover for extra text, inspect Uses, compare slot types and source mod before salvaging, throwing away or spending something irreplaceable."
		"17. Never assume a recipe shown in JEI is currently obtainable. Some components rely on loot, boss drops, dimensions, configured worldgen or disabled crafting routes. The manual will explain confirmed exceptions."
		"18. Store your expedition kit separately. A backpack preset for exploration is often more useful than carrying every building material and technical tool."
		"19. Build around your inventory and control comfort. Place escape, food, healing, main weapon, ranged/spell attack and utility items in places you can use under pressure. The exact arrangement is personal."
		"20. Label storage meaningfully. “Boss drops,” “upgrade materials” and “rare curios” are more useful than 12 unsorted chests when you return with hundreds of modded items."
	]
	task.65462AAA066B8DB6.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.8EEF3441E33CDC62.title: "Combat and equipment — surviving instead of only increasing damage"
	quest.8EEF3441E33CDC62.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.8EEF3441E33CDC62.quest_desc: [
		"Optional practical tips. This page gives no quest rewards and is not required to progress."
		"21. Damage per hit isn't everything. Attack speed, reach, attack animations, recovery windows, spell cast times, armor and enemy movement can make a nominally weaker weapon better for a particular fight."
		"22. Learn a boss's rhythm. A telegraphed attack is a chance to move, block or prepare counterplay. More health cannot compensate for every unavoidable mechanic."
		"23. A shield is valuable, but not omnipotent. Modded bosses may use beams, AoE damage, grabs or other effects that don't behave like a vanilla zombie attack."
		"24. Don't confuse armor points with full durability. Check protection enchantments, armor toughness, actual damage resistance and effects separately."
		"25. Supports need to complement each other. Two A-grade combat supports that work together are better than two stronger-looking ones that occupy the same exclusive slot. They must be equippable at the same time."
		"26. Investigate triggers and cooldowns. Some Relics only help when you take damage, attack, move, accumulate energy or activate them. Test one item against safe mobs before expecting it to save you in a superboss fight."
		"27. Check for hidden tradeoffs. An item with powerful offense may lower defense; an Origin may excel in a particular environment but have a situational weakness. Read the full tooltip."
		"28. Use the training dummy when measuring gear. If available in our final roster, test a few repeatable hits/spells under comparable conditions. One critical hit is not a reliable DPS benchmark."
		"29. Recognize when a dungeon is above your tier. Mark the entrance, remember the danger, upgrade and return. The Explorer's Journal should preserve discovery separately from conquest."
		"30. Use consumables intelligently. Resistance potions, food, movement options and escape tools can matter far more than a tiny increase in weapon rarity."
	]
	task.65462BAA066B8F69.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.8EEF2F41E33CD3E3.title: "Exploration — the pack's actual core progression"
	quest.8EEF2F41E33CD3E3.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.8EEF2F41E33CD3E3.quest_desc: [
		"Optional practical tips. This page gives no quest rewards and is not required to progress."
		"31. Most of the world is worth inspecting, not empty land between bosses. AO combines modded biomes, large dungeons, ruins, villages, bridges, caves, dimensions and environmental mechanics. Listen for unfamiliar enemies and scan silhouettes before rushing."
		"32. Don't judge a structure by size. A tower can be scenic or extremely dangerous. Its name, inhabitant, biome and tier matter more than visual scale."
		"33. Not all structures spawn in all biomes. AO has extensive biome and structure configuration; some sites may be rarer or restricted to particular temperature, height or dimension conditions."
		"34. Ocean exploration requires a different kit. Prepare a boat or ship, light, breathing or movement aids and an escape strategy. Frozen seas and underwater monuments aren't ordinary land dungeons."
		"35. Caves aren't all the same. Alex's Caves adds biome-specific hazards and rewards; finding the correct cave is an expedition in itself. Use the native Cave Compendium/Tablets once their exact mechanics are verified."
		"36. Keep one return marker per dimension. Nether and End coordinate/travel behavior differs from the Overworld. Mark portals and travel hubs in the map you actually use."
		"37. Scenic landmarks can be discoveries too. Outstanding mountains, unusual coastlines and huge caves can be personally worth remembering, even without a chest or boss."
		"38. Your journal shouldn't punish curiosity. You can discover a Tier 7 ruin long before you're equipped to fight inside it. Observe, label and return later rather than forcing progression."
		"39. Do not assume every dungeon has a boss. Some structures are exploration/loot challenges; never search endlessly for a final boss that isn't present."
		"40. Preserve secrets for yourself. An explorer's treasure rumor should point toward an adventure, not automatically reveal the coordinates of every rare structure."
	]
	task.65462CAA066B911C.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.8EEF2E41E33CD230.title: "Magic, progression and optional systems"
	quest.8EEF2E41E33CD230.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.8EEF2E41E33CD230.quest_desc: [
		"Optional practical tips. This page gives no quest rewards and is not required to progress."
		"41. Magic can be practical outside combat. Before farming high-damage scrolls, investigate travel, building, light, control and other utility spells."
		"42. Iron's Spells has separate spell schools and progression mechanics. A book, scroll, mana resource, spell level and casting speed are not the same thing. Use the full Iron's manual to understand how they connect."
		"43. Ars Nouveau spells can be constructed. Start with a targeting form and one simple effect, then understand Source costs, glyph modifiers and rituals before creating expensive chains."
		"44. Apotheosis adds another layer to equipment. Its enchanting, affixes, gems, sockets and reforging offer different choices. Salvage and socket according to your build, not only the item's color."
		"45. One mod can hide a large campaign. NeoPasterDream's puzzles and dimensions, Bumblezone's peaceful hive systems and Enigmatic Legacy's relics are optional but substantial. Never assume a smaller mod lacks progression."
		"46. The Seven Curses route is deliberately optional. Normal Enigmatic Legacy relics have a separate track. Read a verified current-version warning before intentionally accepting irreversible or harsh mechanics; a quest never forces acceptance."
		"47. End Remastered values diverse adventures. Its portal uses different Eye variants from multiple sources. The final manual will list AO-confirmed sources without forcing all 16 Eyes or one impossible route."
		"48. Build identity matters more than a perfect universal weapon. AO's future Origins and Disciplines should complement gear and environment, not force players into a mandatory class. Feel free to experiment."
		"49. Some “powerful” gear is overkill for routine exploration. Keep reliable lower-maintenance travel equipment, and reserve specialist boss gear for actual difficult encounters."
		"50. Read the FTB manual when a system gets technical. Questlog shouldn't interrupt a dungeon story with 20 crafting microsteps. Bookmark the relevant explanation and return to the adventure."
	]
	task.65462DAA066B92CF.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.8EEF3141E33CD749.title: "Multiplayer — good habits for 5–7 friends"
	quest.8EEF3141E33CD749.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.8EEF3141E33CD749.quest_desc: [
		"Optional practical tips. This page gives no quest rewards and is not required to progress."
		"51. Check whether a loot container is personal or shared. Lootr may grant individual dungeon loot, but that does not mean every container or boss drop is duplicated."
		"52. A different Origin or spell school doesn't make someone weaker. Different playstyles should complement each other, not dictate party membership or become mandatory roles."
		"53. Know who's watching the exit. In a crowded dungeon, a safe retreat and regroup point can matter more than everyone chasing the same mob."
		"54. Coordinate around special attacks and effects. AoE spells, summoned entities and combat knockback can make fights harder for friends if poorly timed."
		"55. Respect personal quest progress. We want persistent individual adventure records. A teammate finding a structure or defeating a boss may not complete your own milestone until party credit is verified and configured."
		"56. Share information without spoiling the world. Saying “I found a very dangerous ice dungeon” is different from telling everyone the exact final-boss loot and coordinates."
		"57. Voice/chat controls should be deliberate. AO's default-options source proposes J for microphone mute, but actual personal bindings can differ. Check the Controls screen before your first group expedition."
	]
	task.65462EAA066B9482.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.8EEF3041E33CD596.title: "Performance, troubleshooting and configuration"
	quest.8EEF3041E33CD596.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.8EEF3041E33CD596.quest_desc: [
		"Optional practical tips. This page gives no quest rewards and is not required to progress."
		"58. Slow chunk loading isn't always low FPS. AO's terrain and structure pipeline can be computationally heavy while newly generating the world. A smooth, pre-generated server area behaves differently from sprinting into brand-new terrain."
		"59. Don't increase your render distance blindly. More view distance, shaders, particles and distant terrain each cost resources. First establish stable frame time in a familiar area; then tune one setting at a time."
		"60. Distant Horizons, Voxy and shader add-ons are optional performance/visual experiments. Do not assume both LOD systems run together or that Euphoria Patches can make every renderer compatible; official profiles will be tested."
		"61. Screenshots and precise bug reports help. State your pack version, dimension/coordinates if appropriate, what you were doing and whether the problem reproduces; never paste private multiplayer data into public discussions inadvertently."
		"62. Conflicting keys are normal in a large pack. Look up the action name, rebind overlapping spell/backpack/voice/menu controls, and use the Keybind Cheatsheet."
		"63. If a recipe or structure seems missing, it may be intentionally changed. AO alters biome eligibility, loot, recipes and difficult bosses; use the version-specific guide rather than a video for a different MC version."
		"64. Do not trust command-only or creative-exclusive items as legitimate quest targets. The published questbook should use only items obtainable in the real configured survival game."
		"65. Find the difference between a read-only guide and a rewarded quest. FTB tips are permanent references; Questlog adventure milestones own the actual rewards. Reading a tip doesn't obligate you to complete a tutorial."
	]
	task.65462FAA066B9635.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.8EEF3B41E33CE847.title: "Short “Did you know?” panels to sprinkle throughout the manual"
	quest.8EEF3B41E33CE847.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.8EEF3B41E33CE847.quest_desc: [
		"Optional practical tips. This page gives no quest rewards and is not required to progress."
		"- Did you know? Hover an item and press U in JEI to discover useful crafting paths from what looks like useless loot."
		"- Did you know? Two beautiful structures can have wildly different danger tiers."
		"- Did you know? Some equipment bonuses trigger only under particular conditions, so the tooltip can tell you more than rarity."
		"- Did you know? Leaving a boss arena and returning later is a valid strategy. Discovery is progress too."
		"- Did you know? Your first Origin should shape playstyle, not decide everything your character can ever become."
		"- Did you know? You don't need every End Remastered Eye variant to enter the End if the standard 12-of-16 mechanic remains enabled."
		"- Did you know? AO aims to give every player their own discoveries; a group victory or personal kill may be tracked differently depending on final quest configuration."
		"- Did you know? A new biome may mean entirely different resources, mobs and structure eligibility."
		"- Did you know? Structure-size, loot rarity, armor points and boss tier are four different things."
		"- Did you know? The Field Manual is for questions you have; the Adventure Journal is for journeys you choose."
	]
	task.654630AA066B97E8.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	chapter.83CCD5C1D94E1398.title: "Ambient Odyssey — Tips & Tricks"
	quest.A19534FBE1E8E691.title: "Five controls you'll actually use"
	quest.A19534FBE1E8E691.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.A19534FBE1E8E691.quest_desc: [
		"Optional keybind reference with no rewards. AO settings and keyboard layouts vary. Recheck Options > Controls in your actual client; defaults mentioned here are not guaranteed bindings."
		"- Action — Default / current AO baseline — Why it matters"
		"- Show how to make an item — Hover item → R (JEI default) — Recipe and machine input"
		"- Show what an item is used for — Hover item → U (JEI default) — Figure out why a strange boss drop or material matters"
		"- Find a location on your full-screen map — M (Xaero's World Map default) — Avoid losing a dungeon or portal"
		"- Mark a discovery — B (Xaero's Minimap default) — Create a waypoint before entering danger"
		"- Open accessories — O (AO-distributed Keybind Overrides / DefaultOptions setting) — Manage rings, charms and Curios/Accessories layout"
		"Important: The AO overrides currently define J = mute microphone, O = accessories screen, and FTB Chunks map = unbound. They are present in:"
		"- release_030/overrides/config/defaultoptions/keybindings.txt;"
		"- release_030/overrides/config/keybindoverrides-client.toml."
		"Caution: keybindoverrides-client.toml presently has applyOverrides = false, meaning that source config will not currently force those overrides on next launch. DefaultOptions may still apply them to new profiles. Never call these controls guaranteed for an existing player's customized client until tested. The map keys above are Xaero defaults, not explicit AO overrides."
	]
	task.04BBECF2496D66E4.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.A19533FBE1E8E4DE.title: "Basic inventory and combat"
	quest.A19533FBE1E8E4DE.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.A19533FBE1E8E4DE.quest_desc: [
		"Optional keybind reference with no rewards. AO settings and keyboard layouts vary. Recheck Options > Controls in your actual client; defaults mentioned here are not guaranteed bindings."
		"- Key / interaction — Action — Tip"
		"- E — Open inventory — Access equipment, crafting grid and JEI item list"
		"- Q — Drop one held/hovered item — Be careful near lava, void or other players"
		"- Ctrl + Q — Drop a full hovered stack — Especially dangerous near a boss arena; verify selected/hovers"
		"- F — Swap selected hotbar item with off-hand — Great for quickly switching torches, shield or Totem-style utility"
		"- Shift + Click — Quick-move an item stack to/from container — Often much faster than dragging"
		"- 1–9 while hovering an inventory item — Exchange it with the chosen hotbar slot — Useful when reorganizing mid-expedition"
		"- Double Left Click (inventory) — Gather matching items onto the cursor — Behavior depends on inventory screen/mods"
		"- Right Click when holding shield — Raise shield/use off-hand (context-dependent) — Does not block all magic, AoE or modded special attacks"
		"- Shift — Sneak / reduce edge risk — Useful for ledges, farming and danger signs"
		"- Ctrl while moving — Sprint in vanilla controls — Can be remapped; sprint can also be toggled or double-tapped"
		"- F5 — Cycle third-person and first-person views — Useful for seeing boss positioning and armor appearance"
		"- F1 — Toggle interface visibility — Good for screenshots, not for fights"
		"Minecraft Java defaults. MouseTweaks is installed; AO config enables drag/scroll inventory interactions, so the inventory may support additional click-and-drag or scroll movement depending on screen. Those exact actions need a visual example and final GUI conflict test."
	]
	task.04BBEDF2496D6897.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.A19532FBE1E8E32B.title: "JEI — the built-in encyclopedia"
	quest.A19532FBE1E8E32B.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.A19532FBE1E8E32B.quest_desc: [
		"Optional keybind reference with no rewards. AO settings and keyboard layouts vary. Recheck Options > Controls in your actual client; defaults mentioned here are not guaranteed bindings."
		"- Key / pattern — Action — Why this is powerful"
		"- Hover + R — See recipes that produce the hovered item — Answers “how do I get this?”"
		"- Hover + U — See uses/recipes that consume that item — Answers “what is this for?”"
		"- Ctrl + F — Focus JEI search (default) — Find items from almost any inventory screen"
		"- Ctrl + O — Show or hide JEI item panel (default) — Clear screen space"
		"- @modname search — Narrow to a particular mod — Example: @ars or @apotheosis"
		"- #word search — Search tooltip text (when enabled) — Useful for special effects and item descriptions"
		"- -word search — Exclude a search term — Filter very large mod lists"
		"- A over a JEI item — Bookmark a frequently used item (default if enabled) — Saves trips back through long recipe chains"
		"- JEI + button in recipes — Move eligible ingredients into a crafting grid — Requires the real ingredients and compatible screen"
		"- Recipe navigation arrows / scroll — Navigate alternate recipes — One item can have several sources or machines"
		"Defaults sourced from the JEI developer's 1.21.1-compatible mod page and need an AO GUI regression check. JEI showing a recipe does not guarantee AO allows it: KubeJS, datapacks, Paxi and mod configurations can change recipes/loot. Ask the Field Manual about special machines when a recipe shows a non-standard category."
	]
	task.04BBEEF2496D6A4A.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.A19531FBE1E8E178.title: "Maps, exploring, waypoints"
	quest.A19531FBE1E8E178.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.A19531FBE1E8E178.quest_desc: [
		"Optional keybind reference with no rewards. AO settings and keyboard layouts vary. Recheck Options > Controls in your actual client; defaults mentioned here are not guaranteed bindings."
		"- Key or action — Status — What to learn"
		"- M full map — Xaero's World Map default; verify AO — See explored terrain at a larger scale"
		"- B new waypoint — Xaero's Minimap default; verify AO — Create a marker for home, portals and dangerous discoveries"
		"- Y minimap settings — Xaero's Minimap default; verify AO — Change waypoint rendering and minimap preferences"
		"- FTB Chunks map — AO overrides: deliberately unbound — Use the supported menu/button if you need claims; don't accidentally open a second competing map"
		"- World map / dimension switching — Find in Controls → Xaero; not yet pinned — Map previews of Nether/End depend on map setup and discovered chunks"
		"- Waystone menu — Interact with a Waystone — Teleport rules, fuel and restrictions depend on configured server"
		"- Explorer's Journal and return markers — Future content, no key yet — Personal discovery progress and visited-location bookmarks"
		"Default map keys verified via Xaero Minimap FAQ. Map mods and FTB Chunks may overlap in UI; AO intentionally unbound the FTB Chunks map in its config. Do not reveal undiscovered structure coordinates as a “tip”."
	]
	task.04BBEFF2496D6BFD.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.A19538FBE1E8ED5D.title: "Modded combat, backpacks, RPG and voice"
	quest.A19538FBE1E8ED5D.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.A19538FBE1E8ED5D.quest_desc: [
		"Optional keybind reference with no rewards. AO settings and keyboard layouts vary. Recheck Options > Controls in your actual client; defaults mentioned here are not guaranteed bindings."
		"This is the action lookup table, not a guessed keyboard layout. Fill the final key and tooltip from AO's actual options.txt / DefaultOptions export after the modpack's content roster is frozen."
		"- Mod/system — Important action — Current AO value — How to find/test it"
		"- FTB Ultimine — Hold mining modifier; cycle area/shape — Unverified binding — Options → Controls → Key Binds → FTB Ultimine; AO config enables hold Ultimine + sneak for shape menu; holding Ultimine required to cycle"
		"- Sophisticated Backpacks — Open equipped backpack; trigger enabled backpack upgrades — Unverified — Controls → Sophisticated Backpacks; check worn versus handheld action and conflicting number keys"
		"- Iron's Spells 'n Spellbooks — Cast spell, next/previous equipped spell, radial spell wheel — Unverified — Controls → Iron's Spellbooks; spell wheel toggle was introduced unbound by default in 1.21.1 mod version 3.12.1, so do not promise an assigned key"
		"- Ars Nouveau — Cast/spellbook action, open or cycle spell slots and spell shortcuts — Unverified — Controls → Ars Nouveau and in-game spellbook help; many effects are context sensitive"
		"- Relics / Artifacts — Trigger active relic or accessory ability — Depends on item/mod; unverified — Inspect tooltip and Controls. Many support items trigger passively and have no keybind"
		"- Origins (future) — Primary/secondary active Origin ability — Not configured/installed as approved backend — Add after Origin selection; ensure no overlap with spell casting or backpack toggle"
		"- Questlog (future) — Open Adventure Journal — Not installed / final key unverified — Prefer an easy non-conflicting shortcut or inventory button; engine must be tested"
		"- FTB Quests — Open Field Manual / questbook — AO final binding unverified — Provide persistent menu access; distinguish from Questlog journal"
		"- Accessories — Open accessory GUI — AO distributed suggestion: O — Confirm O survives profile first-launch and Curios/Accessories integration"
		"- Simple Voice Chat — Mute/unmute microphone — AO distributed suggestion: J — Confirm works in multiplayer and cannot accidentally mute during combat"
		"- Simple Voice Chat — Push-to-talk / voice GUI / settings — Unverified — Controls → Simple Voice Chat; set privacy and preferred activation style"
		"- Better Combat / Simply Swords — Special weapon actions and any alternate attacks — Weapon/mod specific, verify — Controls + item tooltip; no universal special-ability key"
		"- Cosmetic Armor / transmog — Toggle vanity appearance UI — Unverified — Inspect actual inventory GUI; don't confuse visual layer with stats"
		"- Backpack + Curios — Any UI launch shortcut collision — Not resolved — Check O against custom backpack, Trinkets/Accessories and Inventory screens"
		"Developer documentation: Iron's Spells changelog records a new unbound-by-default Spell Wheel Toggle keybinding in 3.12.1. This does not prove its final 3.16.x AO binding."
	]
	task.04BBE8F2496D6018.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.A19537FBE1E8EBAA.title: "Debug and visibility — advanced, optional"
	quest.A19537FBE1E8EBAA.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.A19537FBE1E8EBAA.quest_desc: [
		"Optional keybind reference with no rewards. AO settings and keyboard layouts vary. Recheck Options > Controls in your actual client; defaults mentioned here are not guaranteed bindings."
		"- Key — What it does — Use responsibly"
		"- F3 — Debug screen (coordinates and technical data, permission dependent) — Look up the dimension, biome ID and performance metrics during tests"
		"- F3 + G — Chunk borders — Useful when troubleshooting chunk boundaries and claims"
		"- F3 + B — Entity hitboxes and facing direction — Useful for combat testing; turn off after"
		"- F3 + H — Advanced item tooltips — Useful for durability, IDs and debugging gear"
		"- F3 + Q — List supported debug shortcuts — Version and keyboard dependent"
		"- F2 — Screenshot — Share a discovery or reproduce a broken UI (never automatically upload private maps)"
		"Some laptop keyboards require Fn for function keys. Only show debug keys in an Advanced subsection, not as initial must-learn controls."
	]
	task.04BBE9F2496D61CB.title: "Optional: mark page as read"
	quest.A19536FBE1E8E9F7.title: "Keybind conflicts: quick fix"
	quest.A19536FBE1E8E9F7.quest_subtitle: "Optional reference page — no rewards or progression requirements"
	quest.A19536FBE1E8E9F7.quest_desc: [
		"Optional keybind reference with no rewards. AO settings and keyboard layouts vary. Recheck Options > Controls in your actual client; defaults mentioned here are not guaranteed bindings."
		"1. Open Options → Controls → Key Binds and search for the action name, not only the letter. In large modpacks many mods compete for G, R, V, B, Z, the side mouse buttons and spell wheel controls."
		"2. Check whether the conflict is active in the same context: an inventory-only JEI R is not necessarily a collision with world-only gameplay R, but overlapping actions can still misfire."
		"3. Choose an easy-to-remember key for actions you use during combat, then move rarely used menus to distant keys or modifier combinations. Keep familiar Minecraft actions whenever practical."
		"4. For AO, start by checking O Accessories, J voice mute, Xaero M/B, and FTB Chunks map unbound—not by guessing the options on an old profile match the packaged defaults."
		"5. After adding Questlog, new Origins, Traveler's Titles, backpack mods or other expansion content, re-run all keybind screenshots and publish the result here."
		"6. If a key mysteriously does nothing: confirm it is bound, no screen is intercepting it, the item must be equipped if required, you're not sneaking / riding / swimming, and the mod is actually loaded."
	]
